    "# Summary of the Extended Model (Nested Hierarchical)\n",
    "\n",
    "Visual verification of the Posterior Predictive Check demonstrated that the extended model achieves an identical global fit to the baseline model — the posterior replications ($y_{rep}$) correctly capture the core of the flow distribution as well as the right tail of flood events.\n",
    "\n",
    "However, this result is a valuable scientific observation. With the number of observations at $N_s \\approx 300–500$ per station, the likelihood function completely dominates the shrinkage effect originating from the hierarchical level — a phenomenon known in the literature as \"likelihood overwhelms prior\" in a data-rich regime. The partial pooling mechanism has no chance to operate when each station possesses enough of its own data for independent parameter estimation.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Identified Limitations and Directions for Future Research\n",
    "\n",
    " **Stable Physical-Geographical Predictors:** Catchment area and altitude (above sea level) are constant over time and could serve as predictors for the scale parameter $\\sigma_s$, decoupling its estimation from the anomalies of a single baseline year."
   ]
