    "## Prior Predictive Check — Extended Model v2\n",
    "\n",
    "The Prior Predictive Check for the extended model v2 verifies the soundness of the a priori assumptions for the key elements of the model.\n",
    "\n",
    "The distribution $\\mu_{\\text{global}} \\sim \\mathcal{N}(3, 1.2)$ remains identical to previous models; its calibration was intentionally preserved to ensure the comparability of reference points across all three models. The simulated a priori flows fall within a physically plausible range, with a median of $19.22~\\mathrm{m^3/s}$ (approximately $20~\\mathrm{m^3/s}$) and a 99th percentile (representing extreme events) reaching $13{,}090.42~\\mathrm{m^3/s}$.\n",
    "\n",
    "The key novelty of model v2 is the parameter $\\alpha_c \\sim \\mathcal{N}(0, 0.5)$, which controls the effect of the catchment area on the variability scale $\\sigma_s$. The prior is symmetric around zero — the model does not presuppose any direction of the effect (neither that a larger catchment increases nor decreases variability). A standard deviation of 0.5 on the log scale allows the parameter to freely explore values from $-1$ to $+1$, which corresponds to physically interpretable scaling factors. The final posterior value ($\\alpha_c = -0.117$) falls well within the broad a priori span (95% CI: $[-0.921,\\ 0.955]$), meaning that the prior did not artificially constrain the estimation."
