    "# Summary of the Extended Model v2 (Nested Hierarchical with Physical-Geographical Covariate)\n",
    "\n",
    "Visual verification of the Posterior Predictive Check demonstrated that the extended model v2 achieves a global fit identical to the previous models. MCMC convergence remained ideal: $\\hat{R} = 1.00$ for all parameters, no divergences, and satisfactory ESS.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Key Finding: The Catchment Area Effect\n",
    "\n",
    "Introducing the covariate $\\widetilde{c}_s = \\log(\\text{catchment}_s)$ revealed a statistically significant physical-geographical effect:\n",
    "\n",
    "$$\\alpha_c = -0.117 \\quad \\text{(95\\% CI: } [-0.165,\\ -0.065]\\text{)}$$\n",
    "\n",
    "The confidence interval does not contain zero, meaning the effect is significant. The negative direction has a hydrological justification: small mountain catchments (e.g., MYSZYNIEC, ~100 km²) are characterized by higher relative flow variability than large lowland rivers (e.g., TCZEW, ~194,000 km²). This is a well-known hydrological relationship: large catchments aggregate precipitation from a vast area, which smooths out local extremes and stabilizes flow.\n",
    "\n",
    "## Historical Validation (2024 Backtesting)\n",
    "\n",
    "Despite the statistical significance of $\\alpha_c$, the quantitative effect proved too weak to shift alarm thresholds in a way visible during backtesting. The pathologies identified in the baseline model remained unchanged:\n",
