   "source": [
    "Analysis of the shifts in alarm thresholds between the baseline model and version v2 confirms the above conclusion quantitatively. The maximum change in the 95% threshold among all 69 stations was a mere 1.14% (the ŻABNO station), and for the pathological stations, the shifts were below 1% (MYSZYNIEC: +0.90%, PTAKI: +0.03%). Although the catchment area covariate is statistically significant as a model parameter ($\\alpha_c = -0.117$, 95% CI: $[-0.165, -0.065]$), it does not translate into a practical change in alarm thresholds. The effect is too weak relative to the dominant signal from local station data, which once again points to the autocorrelation of time series as a fundamental limitation of the model's architecture."
   ]
  },
